	~		|

Time to Adjust Expectations UE=
	2
	~	Years
	~		|

Time Horizon to Assess Unemployment=
	2
	~	Years
	~		|

Adjustment of Unemployment Expectations=
	(Perceived Unemployment Rate - Reference Unemployment Rate)/Time Horizon to Assess Unemployment
	~	Percent/Year
	~		|

Sensitivity of Unemployment on Wages=
	2
	~	Years [0,20,0.5]
	~		|

Test Switch=
	1
	~	 [0,1,1]
	~		|

Max Effect of Unemployment on Wages=
	1.5
	~	Dimensionless
	~		|

Expected Chg in Unemployment= INTEG (
	Expectations Adjustment Unemployment,
		Initial Exp Chg in Unemployment)
	~	Fraction/Year
	~		|

Effect of Unemployment on Wages=
	2*(Max Effect of Unemployment on Wages-1)/(1+exp((Expected Chg in Unemployment)*Sensitivity of Unemployment on Wages\
		))+(
	2-Max Effect of Unemployment on Wages)
	~	Dimensionless
	~	2*(Max Effect of Wealth on Savings-1)/(1+exp(-(Perceived Wealth Ratio-1)*Sensitivity \
		of Wealth on Savings))+(
		2-Max Effect of Wealth on Savings)
	|

Perceived Unemployment Rate= INTEG (
