	~		|

Prod to Labor Ratio=
	Production/Employed Labor
	~	(Goods/Year)/Person
	~		|

Tax Rate=
	Initial Tax Rate * (1 - Tax Transition) + Final Tax Rate * Tax Transition
	~	Percent
	~		|

Current Net Investment in Capital Units=
	((Private Investment +Gov Investment)/Asset Price)-Capital Consumption
	~	Capital Units/Year
	~	The amount of investment above replacement investment.
	|

Temporary Change in Money Growth Rate=
	0
	~	Percent/Year [-10,10,1]
	~		|

Growth In Money=
	((Money Growth Rate/Percent) + Temporary Shift in Money Growth Rate)*Money Supply
	~	$/Year
	~		|

Time to Start Change in Money Growth Rate=
	3.5
	~	Years
	~		|

Temporary Shift in Money Growth Rate=
	(Temporary Change in Money Growth Rate/Percent)*PULSE(Time to Start Change in Money Growth Rate\
		, Duration of Change in Money Growth Rate )
	~	Fraction/Year
	~		|

Duration of Change in Money Growth Rate=
	2
	~	Years
	~		|

Reference Investment= INITIAL(
	2.7e+06)
	~	Capital Units
	~		|

Reference Production= INITIAL(
	2e+09)
	~	Goods
	~		|

Applied Labor=
	Employed Labor*Work Effort
	~	Person*Years
	~	Translates people employed to person-years of labor applied.
	|

Net Investment=
	Net Investment in Capital Units*Asset Price
	~	$/Year
	~	The amount of investment above replacement investment.
	|

Work Effort=
	1
	~	Person*Years/Person
	~	Defines the average number of person years worked per person per year.  At \
		this time, model does not address overtime.
	|

Time to Acquire Capital Assets=
	3
	~	Years
	~		|

Ref Invest Mult from Initial=
	20
	~	Years
	~		|

Initial Money Supply=
	Employed Labor*Initial Per Worker Money Supply
	~	$
	~		|

Initial Per Worker Money Supply=
	10000
	~	$/Person
	~		|

Savings=
	Savings Fraction*Disposable Income
	~	$/Year
	~		|

Sens of Asset Price to Asset Income Ratio=
	4
	~	Years
	~		|

Sens of Price to Wages Income Ratio=
	4
	~	Dimensionless/(Fraction/Year)
	~		|

Time to Adjust Expectations AIR=
	0.5
	~	Years
	~		|

Adjustment of Asset Income Ratio Expectations=
	(Perceived Asset Income Ratio-Expected Asset Income Ratio)/Time Horizon to Assess Asset Income Ratio
	~	(($/Year)/Capital Units)/Year
	~		|

Sensitivity of Wealth on Savings=
	4
	~	Years [0,20,0.5]
	~		|

Adjustment of Normal Savings Rate=
	(Constrained Savings Fraction - Normal Savings Fraction)/Time to Adjust Savings Norms
	~	Dimensionless/Year
	~		|

Consumption=
	(1-Savings Fraction)*Disposable Income
	~	$/Year
	~		|

Time Horizon to Assess Asset Income Ratio=
	1
	~	Years
	~		|

Normal Savings Fraction= INTEG (
	Adjustment of Normal Savings Rate,
		Initial Savings Rate/Percent)
	~	Dimensionless
	~		|

Change in Asset Income Ratio=
	(Perceived Asset Income Ratio - Expected Asset Income Ratio)/Expected Asset Income Ratio\
		/Time Horizon to Assess Asset Income Ratio
	~	Fraction/Year
	~		|

Asset Price=
	Expected Asset Price*Effect of Asset Income Ratio on Asset Price*Effect of Money Inflation on Price\
		*Effect of Wage Income Ratio on Price
	~	$/Capital Unit
	~		|

Time to Perceive Asset Income Ratio=
	0.5
	~	Years
	~		|

Perceived Asset Income Ratio= INTEG (
	Perception of Asset Income Ratio,
		Asset Income Ratio)
	~	($/Year)/Capital Units
	~		|

Effect of Wealth on Savings=
	2*(Max Effect of Wealth on Savings-1)/(1+exp((Expected Chg in Wealth)*Sensitivity of Wealth on Savings\
		))+(
	2-Max Effect of Wealth on Savings)
	~	Dimensionless
	~	2*(Max Effect of Wealth on Savings-1)/(1+exp(-(Perceived Wealth Ratio-1)*Sensitivity \
		of Wealth on Savings))+(
		2-Max Effect of Wealth on Savings)
	|

Asset Income Ratio=
	Asset Income/Capital Assets
	~	($/Year)/Capital Units
	~		|

Perception of Asset Income Ratio=
	(Asset Income Ratio-Perceived Asset Income Ratio)/Time to Perceive Asset Income Ratio
	~	(($/Year)/Capital Units)/Year
	~		|

Constrained Savings Fraction=
	MIN(Maximum Savings Fraction,Savings Fraction)
	~	Dimensionless
	~		|

Effect of Money Inflation on Price=
	2*(Max Inflation Eff on Price-1)/(1+exp(-(Expected Money Inflation)*Sens of Price to Inflation\
		))+(2-Max Inflation Eff on Price)
	~	Dimensionless
	~	This function creates an S-curve centered on 1 with an input of 0.  The maximum \
		effect is controlled by the Maximum Inflation Effect on Price.  The slope \
		of the effect is controlled by the Sens of Price to Inflation.  With a Max \
		of 1.5, a sensitivity of 5 produces a slightly lower than 1 effect.  A \
		value of 6 produces a slightly higher than 1 effect.
		
		2*(Max Inflation Eff on Price-1)/(1+exp(-(Perceived Inflation)*Sens of Price to \
		Inflation))+(2-Max Inflation Eff on Price)
		
		1 + Perceived Inflation
	|

